chair.revised_idea:
tool-D3r: Link audit of T1's write_copy miss. A zero-training CPU diagnostic on T1_s200 and T1_s201, with B2_s200/s201 as an unseen-input reference only. It is a 2-seed screen with no design claim, kept outside the sealed R1-R4 marks.

Question: at which link does T1's exact copy of a tool result fail, by digit count 1-9? The links are (1) the reader's keys on entry characters, (2) the copy pointer, (3) the copy-versus-vocabulary gate, (4) the cell or register that writes the character.

Setup (nothing in the model changes):
- Load the two T1 checkpoints under models/tool.py with default cfg (n_loops 8) on CPU.
- Replay the exact write_copy oracle (random.Random(f"{id}|{t}") digit strings, same dev rows and subsample) with a copied loop that records, for every copy event:
  - the written string;
  - the oracle string;
  - the intact (calc-true) result string;
  - per cell or register: the copy-attention argmax position and its mass, which is recomputed from q_cp and k_cp because gen_copy does not return it;
  - the gate (1-g) and the decoded character.
- Replay gate (first, nothing else is read until it holds): per-length operand and answer copy reproduce the T1-SCREEN-RESULT table within 2.0 points at every length cell with n >= 100, on both seeds. If not, the harness is wrong.

Arm 1, miss classifier. Each wrong operand or answer string, by length 1-3 versus 4-9, goes into one class:
 (a) equals the intact calc result (model writes its own remembered value instead of copying);
 (b) equals another string in the context (wrong source);
 (c) digit-mix: right source, some characters or the length wrong;
 (d) other.
 Report n per length and Wilson 95% intervals. A length cell with n < 100 on a seed is 'not read'.

Arm 2, pointer and gate audit, per cell j (place from the right) and length:
 - the attention argmax lands on the right character of the right entry;
 - the mean copy share (1-g);
 - decoded cell correct.
 The first link below its mark is the broken one. Operand cells (query W_k(z)+place row j) are tabled next to answer registers (query is the register token) at lengths 1-3, since the same pointer-generator gives 85-93 versus 96-98.

Arm 3, reader on entries, using the D0 metric (diag_d0.py 9-character window ending at the number), on T1's reader via read_texts:
 - strings are 'op a b = r' with r of 1-9 digits, split by entry, with segment labels (result digit versus operand digit);
 - a signed-result stratum (sub results below zero) is report-only;
 - controls: a random-init reader of the same shape, and B2_s200/s201's reader as an unseen-input reference (both report-only).

Arm 4, report-only logging for the later learned 'did my copy work' check:
 - per-cell max attention mass and attention entropy;
 - AUROC for predicting a wrong cell.
 This is a model-internal quantity, so any later use stays deploy-autonomous (untested).

Pass marks, fixed now (labels: predictions are suggested, untested; they come from the T1-SCREEN-RESULT 'Reading', not from anything run):
- P-A (reader intact): Arm 3 window probe >= 99.0 at every place 1-9 and the digit count, on both seeds. Proved wrong: below 97.0 at any place on either seed, because then the reader keys, which span copy relies on, are the broken link, and this goes to the architecture thread before the re-screen is read. 97 to 99 is inconclusive.
- P-B (4+ digit misses are pointer or cell, not a remembered value): at lengths 4-9, at least 80% of misses are class (b) or (c) on both seeds. Proved wrong: class (a) is >= 50% of 4-9 digit misses on either seed.
- P-C (1-3 digit misses): the same split. If class (a) is >= 50% of the 1-3 digit misses on either seed, record that R1 at 1-3 digits is not a copy-position problem and name the follow-up (for example gate or teaching data on random-digit results) before the re-screen. If class (b) or (c) is >= 80%, the pointer fix plausibly covers 1-3 digits.
- P-D (place localisation): Arm 2 pointer hit is below 90% at cells j >= 3 for 4-9 digit events while >= 97% at cells j <= 2 on the same strings. Proved wrong: pointer hit >= 97% at j >= 3 while exact copy stays below 90%, so the break is the gate or the cell, not the pointer.

Nothing here changes Amendment 3's R1-R4 or its proved-wrong line. The audit only says which named follow-up to prepare. Dropped from the original: Stage A on B2_s100/s101 as a gate, the thinker-state digit probe as a pass/fail, the joint-swap eval, the perturbation and incremental-cache checks (a B3 matter; the radius is invalid for insertions), and the 'restart-position' rung.

Rule 10: developer-side measurement only. Rule 4: 2 seeds, a screen. Rule 6: Ben's PC or M1 CPU. Rule 5: dev rows only. Rule 7: nothing trained, no truncation.

chair.plan_guidance:
No test plan for tool-D5 as a mark change. If the report-only diagnostic is picked up as its own idea, the plan must:
(a) change no sealed mark and judge no verdict;
(b) freeze the family map from analyze.py NUMBER_FAMS, STRING_FAMS and COPY_FAMS in a file before it runs;
(c) compute chance baselines from TRAIN answers only, never from dev (rule 5);
(d) name one B2 reference folder (results/33-pc-confirm-b2) and print the first-look re-run beside it as a noise column (B2 s200 reads 0.00 in q33 but 4.26 in the first-look re-run, so one seed's zero-round value is not stable);
(e) use the T1 screen files as they are (loops:0 9.41 and 5.00; donor 4.85 and 4.78), with no relabelling;
(f) tag every claim shown, suggested or untested, and say 'two seeds is a screen' (rule 4);
(g) include a plain-language summary for Ben: zero-round hits mostly come from questions that can be answered by copying a word or guessing a common answer, not from hidden arithmetic, but that is only suggested until the chance baseline is checked.
Keep the small card experiments (B2, T1) separate from the village model (rule 9).

chair.revised_idea:
Rename to 'variant-miss-map' (avoids the D1-D10 part IDs). Probe only, 0 params, no training. Extend custom_io/diag_ledger.py and the extra_evals teacher-forced path (ledger.py:547-590). Run the six q33 checkpoints B2_s200..s205 (scratchpad b2ckpt, sha256 verified) on the full dev variant split (1,320 rows each) on Ben's PC. Use the PC GPU with amp if CPU float32 does not reproduce the stored counts.

Step 0, reproduce. Re-score each checkpoint on variant with is_hit on accepted answers. It must match the stored RESULT.json variant correct count (s200 = 421) to within +-3 rows, else rerun in the training precision. Only then bin.

Step 1, population table (shown denominators from extra.coverage). Per seed and per family, for every variant row: gold mode (NUM, WORD, GEN, from progparse.row_targets, scoring only), has-gold-program, and whether the row carries worked steps. Split 'no program' into (i) by design (the family has no steps, e.g. cipher_map, letter_ops: the model is a talker-only reader there) and (ii) a hand-limit failure (the row has steps but the parser could not label it: more than 7 steps, more than 16 numbers, a number not matched by \d+, |x|>=1e9, inexact DIV). Report rows over each cap and the share of misses they hold. This also reports how much of the miss set comes from rule-7 answer-only training.

Step 2, one label per miss, fixed precedence:
(0) hand limit, as in 1(ii);
(1) wrong mode (argmax lmode vs gold mode);
(2) program rows only, first wrong step against the gold program using the candidate sets (cands_a, cands_b), split into wrong op and wrong operand pointer, from the free run;
(3) program rows, steps right but the answer pointer (argmax lans) points to a slot not holding the gold value. Judge presence of the gold value from the gold program's own result slot, not 'any valid slot' (constants 1, 2, 10, 100 and prompt numbers make 'present' trivially true);
(4) WORD rows, wrong start or end pointer;
(5) GEN rows, first wrong register in units-first order (ledger.py:390). Recompute copy-only mass (1-g)*p_copy[gold char] from q_cp and k_cp, and report the mixture probability of the gold char and the vocabulary-half mass separately. Count copy only on rows whose gold char occurs in the prompt, and report the rest separately;
(6) other.
Report the noexec lesion and the per-seed loops:0 variant beside it (0.0-5.7, a leak floor, not chance).

Step 3, the programme-family test. On variant rows with a gold program (table_calc, div_exact, compare_numbers, arith_bare, backward_solve and others with prog >= 50%), run gold-forced (teacher-forced) and free. Report per-step op and operand accuracy, whole-program accuracy, and a talker check on the gold-forced workspace (argmax lans in the gold answer slots, lmode == gold mode). This separates op writing, free-run compounding and the talker in one forward pass each. Give table_calc, div_exact and compare_numbers their own rows.

Step 4, the input-link test (correlational only, suggested at best). Among teacher-forced op or operand errors on program rows, compare the error rate on rows whose prompt contains a word type absent from the train prompts (computed from the train prompts, not from the generator) with the rate on rows with no such word. Use in_dist teacher-forced accuracy on the same families (about 100) as the sanity reference.

Drop the cipher_map copy mark (cipher_map has no variant rows). If kept at all, pool its in_dist/answer/frame misses over six seeds (about 16 rows) as an anecdote only.
